From: armantark <chuck67322@berkeley.edu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:56:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Play stereo from the rear speakers as well as the front

The TV sends PCM to the soundbar in stereo only, and the soundbar's
upmix puts only room sound in the rear speakers, so voices stay in
front. With the setting on, the player's audio sink plays stereo PCM
as AAC-LC 5.1, encoded by the TV's own AAC encoder, with the left and
right channels copied to the rear pair, through the TV's compressed
passthrough output. Multichannel and compressed audio, tunneled
playback, and outputs that cannot take AAC-LC 5.1 keep upstream's
audio sink, and so does stereo when the AAC output does not open.
